' Set-inclusion Diagram 05 — Conflict-detector removal soundness (GAP-3).
'
' Removing the single-value-cell (consume-then-produce-by-channel) conflict
' predicate is SOUND: everything it would have flagged is a SUBSET of what the
' RETAINED double-consume / same-IO-event race detector already catches, UNION
' the number/foldable channels (which are intrinsically mergeable and safe to
' leave unflagged):
'
'     removed_fires(a,b)  ⊆  retained_conflict(a,b)  ∪  is_number_channel(a,b)
'
' Reason: updating a single-value cell DEFINITIONALLY consumes the cell's base
' datum, so "both branches consume-then-produce on ch" implies "both consumed the
' same base datum on ch" — exactly the retained produces_consumed race (Check #1,
' minus both-mergeable) when ch is a non-number channel; when ch IS a number
' channel it is in produces_mergeable, so neither detector flags it (correct).
'
' Depicted as nested set regions (⊆ by containment). Mirrors Rocq
' ConflictSoundness.removed_subset_retained / conflict_removal_sound and Rust
' merging_logic.rs test removed_predicate_is_subsumed_by_retained_or_number_channel.
'
' Render:
'   plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/merge-algebra/diagrams/05-conflict-detector-venn.puml

@startuml 05-conflict-detector-venn
!theme plain

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  FontName "monospace"
  FontSize 10
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor<<Retained>> #F3E5F5
  BackgroundColor<<Number>>   #EEFAF1
  BorderColor #444444
}
skinparam legendFontName "monospace"
skinparam legendFontSize 10
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam legendBorderColor #666666
skinparam defaultFontName "monospace"
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

title Conflict-detector removal soundness (GAP-3): removed ⊆ retained ∪ number-ch

' Node color legend:
'   lavender (#E1BEE7)  = RETAINED detector universe (Check #1 double-consume)
'   gold     (#FFE082)  = the removed check's NON-number part (⊆ retained)
'   mint     (#C8E6C9)  = number/foldable channels — intrinsically mergeable
'   green    (#A5D6A7)  = the soundness conclusion (nothing lost)
' Edge color legend:
'   purple (#6A1B9A) = subsumption (removed ⟹ retained on non-number channels)
'   green  (#2E7D32) = number-channel exemption (safe to leave unflagged)

package "RETAINED detector — races_for_same_io_event (Check #1)\n  produces_consumed ∩ (non-mergeable): both branches destroyed\n  the SAME base Produce in COMM on a non-number channel" <<Retained>> {
  rectangle "retained_conflict(a,b)\n= ∃ ch. consumes a ch ∧ consumes b ch\n         ∧ ¬ is_number_ch ch" as RET #E1BEE7
  rectangle "removed single-value-cell check ∩ NON-number:\n  svc_update = consume-then-produce on ch\n  ⟹ base datum consumed in BOTH branches\n  ⟹ a produces_consumed race  ⊆  retained ✓" as SUB #FFE082
  RET -[hidden]-> SUB
}

package "Number / foldable channels (IntegerAdd, BitmaskOr)" <<Number>> {
  rectangle "is_number_channel(a,b)\n= ∃ ch. svc_update a ch ∧ svc_update b ch\n         ∧ is_number_ch ch\nintrinsically mergeable (they FOLD):\nneither detector flags them — CORRECT" as NUM #C8E6C9
}

rectangle "removed_fires(a,b)\n= ∃ ch. svc_update a ch ∧ svc_update b ch\n──────────────────────────────────────\nSOUND to drop:  removed_fires  ⊆\n   retained_conflict  ∪  is_number_channel\n(nothing lost — removed_subset_retained)" as CONC #A5D6A7

SUB  -[#6A1B9A,bold]-> CONC : non-number\ncase (subsumed)
NUM  -[#2E7D32,bold]-> CONC : number\ncase (exempt)

legend bottom
  The removed predicate fires only inside RETAINED ∪ NUMBER. On a non-number
  single-value cell, updating consumes the base datum in both branches — the exact
  produces_consumed race Check #1 keeps (the gold subset ⊆ the lavender universe).
  On a number channel both branches are in produces_mergeable, so the "minus
  both-mergeable" filter correctly leaves it unflagged. Rocq removed_subset_retained
  needs NO hidden hypothesis (the consume conjunct is definitional, via andb_prop);
  is_number_ch is an abstract parameter, so the result holds for ANY classifier.
endlegend

@enduml
